<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Barbell Experiment</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To isolate the behavior of attention mechanisms on bottlenecks, we designed a synthetic Barbell graph task.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Graph Construction.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The basic barbell graph consists of two fully connected cliques of size <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=4</annotation></semantics></math>, connected by a single ”bridge” edge. To introduce distraction, we generate variants with additional ”dummy” cliques also connected to the target clique via bridges.</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Basic Barbell:</span> Two cliques (Source and Target) connected by a bridge.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Extended Barbell:</span> One Source clique, one Target clique, and multiple Dummy cliques (1 or 3), each connecting to the Target clique via its own bridge.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Task Definition.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The task is a signal reconstruction problem.</p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Each node has a 16-dimensional feature vector.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Source Node:</span> One node in the Source clique is initialized with a random 16-dim signal vector.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dummy Signal Nodes:</span> A node in each Dummy clique is initialized with a distinct, constant signal vector.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Target Node:</span> One node in the Target clique (the one connected to the bridge) serves as the target.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Other Nodes:</span> Initialized with zero vectors.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Goal:</span> The model must learn to transport the signal from the Source node to the Target node.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Edge Features.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Edges are encoded with discrete types to potentially guide the model (or confuse it in the random case).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="A1.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Edge type encoding for the Barbell graph.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A1.T5.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
